{"title":"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccfcfc9c986178ae5c0512246b8417f66d28fcfa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2^{2014}+2^{2012}}{2^{2014}-2^{2012}} ?\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"39\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a1cb34209fc703a56410ea1be6662fed5b8dda7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ -1 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1  \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{5}{3} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2013 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 2^{4024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"428\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Factoring out, we get: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/e/eeee2f67fe4aef1a8122033c99d889c6beebe095.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2^{2012}(2^2 + 1)}{2^{2012}(2^2-1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"100\" height=\"43\" />.  \n</p><p>Cancelling out the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3bd68f278bd230bb9682ee2e9c61a4f7c0514e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2012}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> from the numerator and denominator, we see that it simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/c/9cc5bb7589fb19dad59fb84b33e729ef9909073c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{5}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"59\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/a/82a0728f1958d4a563515e301c5ffb684408f720.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2^{2012}$\" width=\"69\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Then the given expression is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/7319038e4bdd32268af83f516f2be13b1093d557.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4x+x}{4x-x}=\\frac{5x}{3x}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{5}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"187\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We observe that all the answer choices other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169b8d69bd74a91e72ec43123070d770633a340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> are integer.\n</p><p>Claim: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/c/23c4d76bfa7879ef51309bb1bd05b99acee3e81f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2^{2014}+2^{2012}}{2^{2014}-2^{2012}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"97\" height=\"39\" /> is not an integer.\n</p><p>Proof:\nWe know that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/f/9dfc685c058a3923bc44dc7a591ea65066c69dea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/b/4cb88f59c264ad042fd34adacdacea413164f24c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{gcd}(a,b) = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b135209b0f877dc2eb1fe40dbd09f35b3648f5cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a|b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>So all we need to prove is that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b960482a6a310969dce90c9550ba6a5cffaa47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{gcd}(2^{2014}+2^{2012}, 2^{2014}-2^{2012}) \\neq 2^{2014}+2^{2012} \\text{ or } 2^{2014}-2^{2012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"481\" height=\"21\" />. Since the numerator is larger than the denominator, the only possible case is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54bf51fb7e8d0654872b1884f4e737bfcea7e51b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(2^{2014}+2^{2012}, 2^{2014}-2^{2012}) = 2^{2014}-2^{2012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"361\" height=\"21\" />. We have to prove that this is impossible. Using the Euclidean Algorithm we can simplify to obtain\n\\begin{align*}\n\\gcd(2^{2014}+2^{2012}, 2^{2014}-2^{2012}) &amp;= \\gcd(2^{2014}+2^{2012}-2^{2014}+2^{2012}, 2^{2014}-2^{2012})\\\\\n&amp;= \\gcd(2 \\cdot 2^{2012}, 2^{2014}-2^{2012})\\\\\n&amp;= \\gcd(2^{2013}, 2^{2014}-2^{2012})\n\\end{align*}\nWe notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/8/858496bce2bac1759c02d54a9062cc143baed91e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2014}-2^{2012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" /> can be factored since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3bd68f278bd230bb9682ee2e9c61a4f7c0514e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2012}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> is a common factor. Factoring gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/093b66296496dfd236e52562034250b80f4b5971.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2014}-2^{2012} = 2^{2012}(2^2-1) = 3 \\cdot 2^{2012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"302\" height=\"21\" />. From this we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is a factor of the original expression. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/1/7611375e9f9a9eaca7d867950f18abf1b10a8236.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(2^{2013}, 2^{2014}-2^{2012}) = \\gcd(2^{2013}, 3 \\cdot 2^{2012}) = 2^{2013} \\neq 2^{2012} \\cdot 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"495\" height=\"21\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/3/1d37b2a4f39f307c119f35b02df863f7e20e325b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2014}-2^{2012} \\nmid 2^{2014}+2^{2012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"207\" height=\"21\" />. So the fraction cannot be simplified into an integer. Hence the answer is the only fraction, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffc7368e8e7b77c88b0b4bf732c88c60e27b439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~JerryZYang\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/1ULw0x9XK4o\">https://youtu.be/1ULw0x9XK4o</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2vf843cvVzo?t=545\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2vf843cvVzo?t=545</a>\n</p><p>~sugar_rush\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/C3prgokOdHc\">https://youtu.be/C3prgokOdHc</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A\">2013 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2